  "summary": "Direct transformer-family evidence is narrow: four candidates apply Self-Attention Encoder Models to mapping active wildfire extent. [V0173] is the cleanest match because it evaluates on FireScope and reports AUROC 0.85. [V0174] reports the highest score, F1=0.92, but on ChurnBench; [V0176] reports MAE 0.71 on Atlas-ICU; and [V0175] reports accuracy 0.64 on MetroFlow. These results are not like-for-like because MAE is an error metric while AUROC, F1, and accuracy are higher-is-better scores. Because five IDs are required, [V0171] is appended only as the closest same-topic comparator: it also addresses mapping active wildfire extent and reports F1=0.88 on MetroFlow, but it uses Message Passing Over Relational Graphs rather than a self-attention/transformer method.",
